Bryon Mackay: And so we all got these apps that looked like mini-web pages, because that's what we knew.

31
00:04:53.170 --> 00:05:02.689
Bryon Mackay: And all the apps that we had in the apps were similar to that, were like web pages. And then things started happening. I remember specific libraries coming out.

32
00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:19.140
Bryon Mackay: I remember when Facebook introduced the hamburger menu, and that was just, like, blew everybody's mind. We're like, what a hamburger menu? You gotta be kidding me! That's amazing! Apple had their human interface guidelines that really steered the way that, that… and still influences how mobile apps are today.

33
00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:28.650
Bryon Mackay: But over those years, then we started to identify there are applications that we can do that we've never done before because of a smartphone.

34
00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:35.519
Bryon Mackay: And so, for example, there was no web app to call a random stranger to come pick you up.

35
00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.899
